  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RESTORING MIGRATORY BIRD HABITAT IN THE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposal presents the continuation of a joint, long-term effort to restore the Colorado River Delta, supported by a bi-national partnership of organizations with the goal of restoring and protecting 100,000 acres. This area features 380 species, over 350,000 wintering water birds and over 60,000 ducks and geese. However, there has been a great reduction in water flow, which endangers the existing habitat for water birds.....The project will: purchase the rights to 3.75 million acre feet per year of water, to restore 988 wetland acres; continue local outreach efforts; and implement a monitoring program to assess the impact of the increased water. ....Species that will benefit include northern pintail, mallard, cinnamon teal, redhead American wigeon, long-billed curlew, snowy plover, least tern, black skimmer, black rail and least bittern...</narrative>
  </description>
